{
  "date": "2026-11-05",
  "source_snapshot": "signature-focus-accepted",
  "scope": "Real OS focus transitions from detached editor to primary window, back to editor, to a separate helper process and back. C/Physim model, analysis and file editors. Actual child blur and peer focus acknowledgement, closed completion list, no painted HUD while unfocused, unchanged source/caret/selection anchors/editor scroll, active SDL text channel and subsequent scripted input. Additional real nonempty selection preserved across a primary/child focus roundtrip. Existing main/child signature and drag workflows remain included.",
  "product_changes": "Detached source window remembers its actual source owner before transient completion cleanup and restores it only on real OS focus gain, if it is still the active target and search does not own input. Clear remembered owner on return/reopen. Use normal editor ownership path, not a forced SDL input channel.",
  "test_fixture_corrections": [
    "First probe wrongly treated the internal signature_visible eligibility/cache flag as actual visibility. The existing renderer already pauses on real focus loss. Final assertion observes zero HUD geometry and no painted signature/footer bytes.",
    "Second probe attempted manual completion after a numeric literal. ps_completion_prepare deliberately rejects that position. Final sequence leaves the list open at its valid original argument position before changing focus.",
    "The first final attempt overlaps Windows and Linux WSLg windows. Linux lacked the requested primary-window focus and its source changed; the main signature group also lost actual focus. These Linux results are not a valid product counterexample. The fixed Linux run uses a private Xvfb/Openbox desktop. The Windows counterexample does have actual returned child focus with its text channel stopped."
  ],
